2026-08-18T16:54:02.8109958Z     
2026-08-18T16:54:02.8110223Z     The ``pytest`` framework makes it easy to write small tests, yet
2026-08-18T16:54:02.8110704Z     scales to support complex functional testing for applications and libraries.
2026-08-18T16:54:02.8111101Z     
2026-08-18T16:54:02.8111300Z     An example of a simple test:
2026-08-18T16:54:02.8111546Z     
2026-08-18T16:54:02.8111744Z     .. code-block:: python
2026-08-18T16:54:02.8111979Z     
2026-08-18T16:54:02.8112200Z         # content of test_sample.py
2026-08-18T16:54:02.8112458Z         def inc(x):
2026-08-18T16:54:02.8112683Z             return x + 1
2026-08-18T16:54:02.8112901Z     
2026-08-18T16:54:02.8113076Z     
2026-08-18T16:54:02.8113260Z         def test_answer():
2026-08-18T16:54:02.8113501Z             assert inc(3) == 5
2026-08-18T16:54:02.8113732Z     
2026-08-18T16:54:02.8113902Z     
2026-08-18T16:54:02.8114080Z     To execute it::
2026-08-18T16:54:02.8114284Z     
2026-08-18T16:54:02.8114464Z         $ pytest
